1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,890
Hi guys.

2
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:03,750
Today, let's talk about LinkedIn.

3
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:07,340
How to create a perfect LinkedIn profile.

4
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:10,530
And also we're going to learn about past simple.

5
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:14,360
How to make it and when to use this tense.

6
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:15,530
Let's go.

7
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,930
So what is LinkedIn?

8
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:23,990
LinkedIn is the world's largest professional network on the Internet.

9
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:32,090
You can use LinkedIn to find the right job or internship, connect with other professionals and exchange

10
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:32,970
messages.

11
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:35,450
You can read about professional news.

12
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,610
Join groups, for example.

13
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:39,410
Net developers community.

14
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:46,130
And you can write articles, post pictures and videos and links to your portfolio.

15
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:52,950
So what are the three most important factors for a successful profile?

16
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:56,010
First one, it's a professional picture.

17
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:02,730
Second, it's catchy headline and informative about section.

18
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:07,800
Catchy headline means easy to remember noticeable headline.

19
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,770
All right, Let's have a look at the screen from my profile.

20
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:16,610
So this is my profile picture.

21
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:22,800
I look into the camera and this picture is quite okay for LinkedIn.

22
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:28,380
Here is my headline, head of people at DJ Digital.

23
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:31,890
I love to bring the best talents to the great team.

24
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:36,120
And here I also added a background picture.

25
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:39,990
In my case, it's a logo of my company.

26
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:46,740
Okay, so headline, it's important to include your job title here.

27
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,870
It's software developer.

28
00:01:49,170 --> 00:01:57,420
Next, your current company, add Google and add some keywords or additional information.

29
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:01,590
For instance, Ray is a mentor and teacher.

30
00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:09,090
All right, about Section, it's a summary of your experience and skills.

31
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:14,700
You should include your achievements there and add some personal story.

32
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:17,530
Okay.

33
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:26,530
Also, it is worth including your skills into your profile, some certificates and courses.

34
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:34,330
And you can also ask people to endorse you to say that you are good at this or that skill.

35
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:36,960
All right.

36
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:45,160
Let's have a closer look at my summary on LinkedIn to describe my past experience.

37
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:55,210
I say I started as an English teacher in it, and then I moved to the HR field and I still absolutely

38
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:59,530
love both jobs hired and Onboarded.

39
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:04,060
More than 60 people organized five team buildings.

40
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:13,000
Okay, here I used past tense to talk about my experience in the past.

41
00:03:15,350 --> 00:03:15,880
Okay.

42
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:19,870
I started my career in 2015.

43
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:23,030
She graduated five years ago.

44
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:27,310
These sentences are in past simple.

45
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:35,750
We take a subject I or she and add a verb with ending e d.

46
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:41,780
These verbs are regular, so we just add ending e d.

47
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:54,560
But sometimes we can have irregular verbs like I forgot to send this letter or she sent me five messages.

48
00:03:54,680 --> 00:04:01,550
For irregular verbs you have to check the table of the irregular verbs.

49
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,030
Okay.

50
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,350
This is a table.

51
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:07,000
And for past simple.

52
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,010
You need to use the second column of the table.

53
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:14,110
If you don't have the table, just Google.

54
00:04:14,110 --> 00:04:16,360
Just type the word for example.

55
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:20,200
But and write regular or irregular or.

56
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,000
But free forms.

57
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,840
And Google will help you find out the free forms.

58
00:04:26,050 --> 00:04:28,840
Okay, Let's have a look at sentences in past.

59
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:29,590
Simple.

60
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:33,270
I worked at Microsoft.

61
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:36,870
I did not work at Microsoft.

62
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:39,360
Did I work at Microsoft?

63
00:04:39,690 --> 00:04:40,050
Okay.

64
00:04:40,050 --> 00:04:44,370
For negative sentence and for a question, we use auxiliary.

65
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:48,420
Did she studied French?

66
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:51,120
She did not study French.

67
00:04:51,150 --> 00:04:53,190
Did she study French?

68
00:04:53,550 --> 00:04:54,320
All right.

69
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:58,950
Pause this video and repeat the sentences for a couple of times.

70
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:03,990
More tips for a successful LinkedIn profile.

71
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,990
Put in the time to make it awesome.

72
00:05:06,990 --> 00:05:11,340
That means spend enough time working on your profile.

73
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:13,800
Get a custom URL.

74
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:16,560
This is your LinkedIn address.

75
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:22,530
Without any additional symbols or numbers, you can do that in settings.

76
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:25,500
Choose a great professional photo.

77
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:29,460
Write a headline that looks impressive.

78
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,590
Exciting and easy to remember.

79
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,530
Headline.

80
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:35,000
Don't waste the summary space.

81
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:38,260
Include your experience skills.

82
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:45,130
Make your summary informative and professional numbers right up front.

83
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:49,390
For example, I say I hired 50 people.

84
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:57,880
A developer developed ten iOS applications, so use numbers to prove your achievements.

85
00:05:58,210 --> 00:06:00,310
Avoid buzzwords.

86
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:04,900
Buzzwords are words that are overused on LinkedIn.

87
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:06,250
For example.

88
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:09,150
Passionate, creative, successful.

89
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:15,310
It's okay to use them once or twice, but don't use them too often.

90
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:18,400
Treat your profile like your resume.

91
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:20,720
So include your skills experience.

92
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:24,910
Keep it professional, but use the first person.

93
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:28,030
Say I created, I developed.

94
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:32,880
I achieved and highlight your skills.

95
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:38,580
Include your main skills, make them visible and ask people to endorse you.

96
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:40,230
All right.

97
00:06:40,590 --> 00:06:47,520
Now you can actually go and try creating your professional LinkedIn profile.

98
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:49,290
Thank you and bye.
